# Alpha

Pins subpagesAlphabetic()'s window-then-sort order: date order (newest
first) is D, C, B, A, so the date-order window is [D, C] / [B, A], and
each window is then alpha-sorted to [C, D] / [A, B]. A sort-then-window
regression would instead compute the full alpha order [A, B, C, D] first
and window THAT, producing [A, B] / [C, D] -- a full swap of both pages,
not a subtle reordering, so it fails loudly.
